### Debounce Function in JavaScript

```javascript
function debounce(func, delay) {
  let timerId;

  return () => {
    clearTimeout(timerId);
    timerId = setTimeout(() => {
      func();
    }, delay);
  };
}
```

---

### Explanation of Usage

The `debounce` function is used to prevent unnecessary re-renders or function calls when a user clicks or interacts with an element multiple times. It delays the execution of the function until the user stops interacting.

